s detector signal matters)\n- Detect-and-remove: -0.005 (hard filtering ineffective)\n- Golden Ratio oracle (requires known ρ): 17.640 (only 0.01 better than adaptive)\n\nTable 5 (τ sweep): Robust in [0.6, 0.8], degrades at boundaries (τ=0.5: under-reweight, τ≥0.9: over-reweight)\n\nTable 6 (n_min sensitivity, batch_size=4): Sharp cliff at n_min=3, n_min≥4 collapses to uniform\n\nTable 7 (Batch size): bs=8 and bs=16 → PPL 17.64, n_min knife-edge vanishes\n\nTable 8 (ρ=0.6): Uniform degrades super-linearly (17.69→18.50). Adaptive improvement amplifies only 1.25× (ESS tightens)\n\nTable 9 (Cross-model): Llama-3.2-3B shows 2× relative improvement (0.444% vs 0.226%), b* median nearly identical (0.85 vs 0.88)\n\nTable 10 (Detector quality): ModernBERT AUC 0.986 vs TF-IDF 0.939 → only 0.005 PPL difference\n\nTable 11 (Cross-generator): Improvement drops from 0.04 to 0.03 PPL\n\nTable 12 (Downstream): MMLU +0.15 (not significant), HellaSwag +0.30 (marginal)\n\nDomain-skewed contamination: improvement drops to 0.02 PPL (~50% of uniform-injection ratio)\n\n**Experimental design reference (from review_context.yaml):** The full experimental design includes these imagined experiments with expected results:\n- Extended grid-b low (b=0.1/0.2/0.3) across 3 seeds — confirms flat PPL landscape\n- ρ=0.6 experiments — effect amplification limited (1.25×)\n- n_min ablation (1-5) — knife-edge at n_min=3 is batch_size=4 artifact\n- ESS-only baseline — Δ=0.01 vs dual, statistically indistinguishable\n- τ sweep — robust in [0.6, 0.8], boundary degradation\n- Golden Ratio oracle — adaptive approaches oracle without knowing ρ\n- Batch size 8/16 — n_min knife-edge vanishes, PPL converges at bs=8\n- ModernBERT detector — AUC +5% yields only 0.005 PPL\n- Cross-generator (Llama-3.2-1B) — improvement drops to 0.03\n- Llama-3.2-3B cross-model — 2× relative improvement, b* distribution stable\n- Detect-and-remove baseline — largely ineffective\n- Random reweighting — confirms detector signal is necessary\n- Domain-skewed (code-heavy) — method's weakest setting (~50% ratio)\n- Downstream eval (MMLU/HellaSwag) — not significant at 200M tokens\n\nThe paper covers most of these experiments. Check coverage completeness.\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nEvaluate:\n1. **Methodological soundness**: Is the dual-constraint formulation correct? Is the minimum-intervention principle well-motivated? Are there flaws in the mathematical framework?\n2. **Experimental rigor**: Statistical significance, number of seeds, baselines, ablations, hyperparameter sensitivity coverage\n3. **Claim-evidence alignment**: Do the experimental results actually support the three stated claims? Are claims overclaimed or appropriately calibrated?\n4. **Reproducibility**: Is there enough detail to reproduce?\n5. **Weaknesses in experimental design**: What's missing? What could undermine the conclusions?\n\nProvide your review in this format:\n\n### Summary (2-3 sentences)\n\n### Strengths (bulleted)\n\n### Weaknesses (bulleted, with severity: Major/Minor)\n\n### Questions for Authors\n\n### Missing Experiments or Analysis\n\n### Claim-by-Claim Assessment\n- Claim 1: ...\n- Claim 2: ...\n- Claim 3: ...\n\n### Preliminary Score: X/6\n### Confidence: X/5\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01EQjrX3hxMJpDMo98nDjPHo","session_id":"bd81513d-34ac-46ce-a706-72967144b268","uuid":"178baed0-602b-4c2f-ae6e-d78cec05477c","timestamp":"2026-05-15T11:08:24.164Z"}
